modifier_claims.support_quote:
A 35-year-old man with a medical history of alcohol use disorder, episodes of renal failure, anemia, thrombocytopenia, and pancreatitis presented with acute alcoholic pancreatitis. He reported abdominal pain and emesis but no bloody diarrhea. Patient has a history of recurrent episodes.

Physical examination revealed diffuse abdominal tenderness.

